        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Appeal to Reason\n- Organizations: Farmers' Alliance, Populist Party\n- People: Julius Wayland, Leonidas L. Polk\n- Places: American Midwest\n- Topics: socialism, agrarian economic movements, left-wing politics\n\nFacts:\n- The Farmers' Alliance was an organized agrarian economic movement among American farmers that developed and flourished in 1875.\n- Appeal to Reason was a weekly left-wing political newspaper published in the American Midwest from 1895 until 1922.\n- Julius Wayland is most noted for publishing Appeal to Reason, a socialist publication often deemed the most important socialist periodical of its time.\n- Leonidas L. Polk was a leader of the Farmers' Alliance and helped found the Populist Party.",
